00:08:29.100 --> 00:08:35.520
Mayuko: Because Japanese manufacturers still held power in
Japan over the last 30 years. There is this bias that

00:08:35.520 --> 00:08:41.490
hardware is first class. Because unlike software, it was
something that you could see and touch.

00:08:41.730 --> 00:08:48.360
Kenji: My main point is that Japanese big companies were
putting the software people in the second class, the first

00:08:48.360 --> 00:08:57.210
class people are hardware. Those who are doing "monozukuri",
or those who are creating actual things, not bits. It's

00:08:57.210 --> 00:08:59.430
tangible. Those things have to be tangible.

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:05.370
Mayuko: For a country that's still very true to like its
craftsmanship roots, this made a ton of sense to me. Japan

00:09:05.370 --> 00:09:12.480
still prides itself in its handmade and multi generational
crafts. Like in America, like stationery stores and

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:19.650
bookstores are like all the disappearing. And that's kind of
true Japan as well, but like they still sell lots of paper

00:09:19.650 --> 00:09:26.190
calendars at the stationery store. And I think that's part
of this bias towards like analog products and like paper.

00:09:26.250 --> 00:09:32.130
And I mean, like regardless of if you're Japanese or not,
concepts that are ambiguous, like the ones that you can't

00:09:32.130 --> 00:09:39.450
like engage all of your senses in like you can't see and
touch and smell it and stuff can be difficult to grasp. So

00:09:39.450 --> 00:09:46.920
this bias against software basically led to low salaries and
poor stock options in tech companies. And adjacent to that

00:09:46.950 --> 00:09:53.250
are labor laws in Japan. They make it really hard for
companies to fire or lay off its employees, which you know,

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:59.220
is great for job security, like Silicon Valley definitely
can't offer that level of job security to anyone. But that

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:06.420
basically creates a lack of a pool of senior talent. And so
companies aren't even really like trying to like hire like

00:10:06.420 --> 00:10:12.480
great people, I guess. So they're not going to offer things
like better benefits or like better projects, because most

00:10:12.480 --> 00:10:18.150
of the hiring that they're doing is straight out of college.
And so as a result of all of this, like Eric mentioned,

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:24.090
software is something that is seen to be outsourced to
someone else because of its second class state.

00:10:29.550 --> 00:10:35.640
Of course, while all this is happening in Japan, and
companies like Google, Apple and Facebook, were taking the

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:42.600
world by storm in America. Silicon Valley charged forward in
creating products and services and companies and

00:10:42.600 --> 00:10:49.170
